+
+
+.. _hookimpl_arg_default:
+
+Hookimpl argument defaults
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+A *hookimpl* can also declare a default value for an argument. The value the
+*hookimpl* receives for such an argument is, in order of precedence:
+
+1. the value passed by the hook call,
+2. the :ref:`hookspec's default value <hookspec_arg_default>`,
+3. the *hookimpl*'s own default value.
+
+The *hookimpl*'s default is therefore only used when neither the caller nor
+the *hookspec* provides the argument. This allows a plugin to use a newly
+added argument while still working with an older version of the host program
+whose *hookspec* does not have the argument yet:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    @hookspec
+    def myhook(config, args):
+        pass
+
+
+    @hookimpl
+    def myhook(config, args, new_arg="fallback"):
+        print(new_arg)
+
+
+    # Older hookspec without new_arg; the hookimpl gets new_arg="fallback".
+    pm.hook.myhook(config=config, args=args)
+
+This applies to plain *hookimpls* and to both kinds of
+:ref:`wrappers <hookwrappers>`.
+
+.. versionchanged:: 1.7
+    A value passed by the hook call, or a *hookspec* default, now takes
+    precedence over the *hookimpl*'s default. Previously the *hookimpl*'s
+    default was always used.
 
 
